BBUUGGSS
       Before glibc 2.16, the following bugs existed in the glibc
       implementation of these functions:

       •  The  domain  error case where _x is 0 or a NaN did not cause _e_r_r_n_o to
          be set or (on some architectures) raise a floating‐point exception.

       •  The domain error case where _x is an infinity did not cause _e_r_r_n_o  to
          be set or raise a floating‐point exception.

